answer: (r, c) | path[::-1]
wrong[(r, c) | path]: The walk starts at the goal, so the path comes out backwards: from (2, 2) to (0, 0). Reverse it.
wrong[start | path[::-1]]: Every cell's parent would be the start, so the walk back jumps straight from the goal to the start: [(0, 0), (2, 2)]. Each parent must be the cell that found it.
