- Take the cell at the front of the queue.
- Give each open neighbour that has no distance yet a distance one bigger, and add it at the back.
- When E is taken out of the queue, its distance is the answer.
hint: The search can't begin until it knows where S is.
hint: The answer is only ready once E leaves the queue.
right: Find the start and exit, seed the queue with S, then repeat: take the front cell and add its new neighbours, until E comes out with its distance.
